    39	- [ ] **Step 3: peer-review SKILL.md에 병합.** `## Finding Triage` 섹션 바로 앞에 삽입 (핵심 규율 압축본, 유실 금지 항목: 성과적 동의 금지·검증 우선·불명확 항목 전체 클라리파이·한 항목씩 구현·기술적 pushback·GitHub 스레드 답글):
    40	
    41	```markdown
    42	## Receiving Review Feedback
    43	
    44	When feedback arrives — from your human partner, a peer reviewer, or GitHub:
    45	
    46	1. READ all items without reacting. If any item is unclear, stop and ask before
    47	   implementing any of them — items may be related, and partial understanding
    48	   produces wrong implementations.
    49	2. VERIFY each claim against codebase reality before implementing.
    50	3. RESPOND technically. Never performatively agree — no "You're absolutely
    51	   right!", no "Great point!", no gratitude. State the requirement, ask, push
    52	   back with evidence, or just fix it: the diff is the acknowledgment.
    53	4. IMPLEMENT one item at a time — blocking issues, then simple fixes, then
    54	   complex ones — testing each before the next.
    55	5. PUSH BACK with technical reasoning when a suggestion breaks existing
    56	   functionality, lacks context, violates YAGNI (grep for actual usage first),
    57	   or conflicts with your human partner's architectural decisions. If you
    58	   pushed back and were wrong, state the correction factually and move on.
    59	
    60	For GitHub inline review comments, reply in the comment thread
    61	(`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/comments/{id}/replies`), not as a
    62	top-level PR comment.
    63	```
