   178	<!-- Adapted from ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT) — condensed and adapted for jstack -->
   179	
   180	Scope: **conversational and status output only.** Artifacts — specs, plans,
   181	docs, commit messages, code comments, review reports — follow their owning
   182	skill's fidelity requirements, not this contract.
   183	
   184	1. Lead with the verdict or action. No warm-up context before the point.
   185	2. Number multi-step work. Keep lists to 5 items or fewer.
   186	3. When a turn advances multi-step work, end with 1-2 lines: current position →
   187	   next step. Include the Linear issue ID when the work is linked to one. Skip
   188	   this on short Q&A turns.
   189	4. Suppress tangents — unrequested side topics get one line at most.
   190	5. Give effort sizing (S/M/L) and the next checkpoint instead of time estimates.
   191	6. On errors and failures: calm, factual tone. No repeated apologies.
   192	7. No closing filler — no "hope this helps," no pleasantries.
   193	
   194	Exceptions override rules: when the user asks for explanation, when ambiguity
   195	needs a clarifying question, and when a destructive action needs confirmation.
   196	```
